df28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-6832/selection/ma-v1/3f137cd2c94f1df7872de8fb3c2c74374f690a572c1c1cfad972dbbc8589b7b5/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-6832/selection/ma-v1/3f137cd2c94f1df7872de8fb3c2c74374f690a572c1c1cfad972dbbc8589b7b5/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-6832/selection/ma-v1/3f137cd2c94f1df7872de8fb3c2c74374f690a572c1c1cfad972dbbc8589b7b5/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-6832"] :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}),\\,\\,\\,y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}),\\,-3\\le t\\le 3,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $0$ | $b$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $c$ |\n| $y$ | $a$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $-1$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $-a+b+c.$" :question/worked-solution "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{3}).$ This gives\n\n$$\na=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi (-3)}{3})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )=-1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi (-1)}{2})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=-1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=3$ into $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi (3)}{2})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n-a+b+c=-(-1)+(-1)+(-1)=-1.\n$$" :question/answer-fields ["q-6832/selection/ma-v1/3f137cd2c94f1df7872de8fb3c2c74374f690a572c1c1cfad972dbbc8589b7b5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-123783"] :question/worked-solution "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x=1-2t.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $5$ | $3$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-3$ | $-5$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=t.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $5$ | $3$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-3$ | $-5$ |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/assets/ef5f33b74b59b5a62fd8670a8feb6487b01a97aed4a44a098a576d10d891bd68.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-16191"] :question/worked-solution "We need to create a table of values and then sketch the curve. First, we work out the $x$-values using the formula $x={t}^{2}.$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ | $16$ | $25$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=t(5-t).$ This gives\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ | $16$ | $25$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $4$ | $6$ | $6$ | $4$ | $0$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038739/assets/1aa848f287660c0858d5d6478da71c5baab9252c13f0a2d4a48c38d61f6bce51.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-16196/selection/0a006121f1aa4a2180835c45086051a6da9bd25c65fd782f0eae572e237d32c7" :answer/id #uuid "b856d