:answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-327861/field-6/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-327861/field-6/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327861" :question/id #uuid "3cab7f67-2e11-5804-8545-2c922e781e01" :question/math-academy-id "q-327861" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhat are the ranges of $x$ and $y?$\n\nThe range of $x$ is \n{{field-1}} $\\le $\n$x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}.\n\n \n\nThe range of $y$ is \n{{field-4}}\n$\\le y$\n{{field-5}}{{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have \n$-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ -6 & \\le 6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\le 6 \\\\ -6 & \\le x\\le 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-6\\le x\\le 6.$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that for $0\\le \\theta <2\\pi ,$ we have \n$-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1.$ Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 1 \\\\ 3 & \\text{ }\\ge -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\text{ }\\ge -3 \\\\ -3 & \\le -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\le 3 \\\\ -3 & \\le y\\le 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can conclude that $-3\\le y\\le 3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-327861/field-1" "q-327861/field-2" "q-327861/field-3" "q-327861/field-4" "q-327861/field-5" "q-327861/field-6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cddc940d-2185-569c-a62b-b507e95d3c35"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327861"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/va